From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GDmio <zhalin66@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:35:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] BlueOS: soong_ui: pass SOONG_GOMEMLIMIT / SOONG_GOGC to
 soong_build

soong_build runs under env -i, so Go's GOMEMLIMIT / GOGC never reach it. On a 32 GB PC the analysis
grew to ~60 GB (the heap reaches twice the live data before a collection) and was OOM-killed. A memory
limit makes the collector work harder instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I024e6e04e91241c053e9221774e5d9de7b376814
---
 ui/build/soong.go | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/build/soong.go b/ui/build/soong.go
index 4521b4abe..5478ff085 100644
--- a/ui/build/soong.go
+++ b/ui/build/soong.go
@@ -230,6 +230,15 @@ func (pb PrimaryBuilderFactory) primaryBuilderInvocation(config Config) bootstra
 		// https://github.com/golang/proposal/blob/master/design/24543-non-cooperative-preemption.md
 		invocationEnv["GODEBUG"] = "asyncpreemptoff=1"
 	}
+	// BlueOS: soong_build runs under `env -i`, so Go's own GOMEMLIMIT / GOGC never reach it. On a 32 GB PC
+	// the analysis grew to ~60 GB (Go lets the heap reach twice the live data before collecting) and was
+	// OOM-killed; SOONG_GOMEMLIMIT (e.g. 30GiB) makes the collector work harder instead of growing.
+	if v := os.Getenv("SOONG_GOMEMLIMIT"); v != "" {
+		invocationEnv["GOMEMLIMIT"] = v
+	}
+	if v := os.Getenv("SOONG_GOGC"); v != "" {
+		invocationEnv["GOGC"] = v
+	}
 
 	var allArgs []string
 	allArgs = append(allArgs, pb.specificArgs...)
